@prefix rdf:           <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:          <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:           <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix skos:          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dct:           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix la:            <https://linked.art/ns/terms/> .
@prefix crm:           <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/> .
@prefix dig:           <http://www.ics.forth.gr/isl/CRMdig/> .
@prefix sci:           <http://www.ics.forth.gr/isl/CRMsci/> .
@prefix crminf:        <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/extensions/crminf/> .
@prefix aat:           <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/> .
@prefix wikidata:      <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/> .
@prefix prov:          <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix time:          <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#> .
@prefix hg:            <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/> .

#####################################################################
# HeritageGraph  ↔  LUX (Linked Art / CIDOC-CRM)  alignment ontology
#
# Companion to HeritageGraph.ttl  (CAIRNepal/heritagegraphontology, main branch,
#               release 1.1.0)
# Version     : 1.1.0 (November 2026), versionIRI
#               <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/alignment/lux/1.1.0>
# Author      : Semih Yumuşak, May 2026
# Contributor : Niraj Karki (CAIR Nepal) — orphan fix (§4) + OWL/DL cleanup,
#               June 2026; sync to HeritageGraph 1.0.0 and 1.1.0 (see the
#               official copy at heritagegraph-lux-migration/alignment/ in the
#               heritagegraphontology repo, main branch, 1.1.0)
# Goal   : LUX → HG migration. LUX records are JSON-LD whose @context
#          maps short names ('HumanMadeObject', 'Person', …) to
#          *crm:* / *dig:* / *sci:* URIs (the real URIs that appear in
#          the data after parsing). Only a handful of classes are
#          genuinely under the la: namespace — namely la:Set,
#          la:Transfer, la:Payment, la:Addition, la:Removal,
#          la:RightAcquisition, la:DigitalService.
#
# Therefore this alignment binds HG classes to the actual URIs LUX uses
# (mostly crm:Enn) and only uses la: for the seven genuine la:-only
# classes. Each comment shows the LUX JSON-LD alias for traceability.
#
# July 2026 (alpha5 regeneration, HeritageGraph branch, commit 2286a6e /
# generated 2026-07-22): the core ontology stopped minting separate
# hg: URIs for 12 classes that map 1:1 onto an external term
# (class_uri in HeritageGraph.yaml now points directly at the crm: URI).
# The former HeritageGraph classes Person, HumanMadeObject, Actor, Place,
# TimeSpan, Material, Production, DestructionEvent, TransferOfCustody,
# ConditionAssessment, ConditionState and Technique no longer exist as
# distinct resources — the crm: URI itself is the HG class now. This
# file (and the migration templates in ../queries/ and ../scripts/) were
# updated to reference those crm: URIs directly instead of the retired
# hg: wrapper. See §6 below for the full note.
#
# Source (October 2026): imported from CAIRNepal/heritagegraph-lux-migration,
# alignment/heritagegraph-lux-alignment.ttl at commit 6772240 (2026-07-26), and
# migrated to the v1.0.0 core: namespace https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/,
# camelCase property names, official CRMinf namespace, no logical axioms
# whose subject is an external term, no equivalence to external classes
# (Activity, Concept, HistoricalEvent now rdfs:subClassOf; Deity ≡ crm:E28 and
# CalendarSystem → crm:E29_Designated_Reference_System removed), no enumeration
# under Concept, mappings on properties whose core IRI already is the CRM
# property dropped as redundant, and hadParticipant ≡ crm:P11 replaced by
# skos:closeMatch. LUX-facing targets follow the Linked Art JSON-LD context
# (sci: = http://www.ics.forth.gr/isl/CRMsci/, as LUX data is serialised).
#
# 1.1.0 (November 2026): follows HeritageGraph 1.1.0. Groups, deaths and
# generic activities are migrated by direct reuse of crm:E74_Group,
# crm:E69_Death and crm:E7_Activity (hg:Group, hg:Death and hg:Activity are
# deprecated, §6); terms this module mints are marked rdfs:isDefinedBy it
# (§8); the module is checked to be conservative over the core
# (evaluation/reasoning_extras.py lux-conservativity). Some §1/§2 axioms
# restate axioms the core already has (e.g. Guthi ⊑ crm:E74_Group): the
# validation queries V1/V4 look only inside the alignment named graph, so
# they are kept here. See CHANGELOG.md [1.1.0].
#
# Apply with:  owl:imports  or  cat alignment.ttl >> HeritageGraph.ttl
#####################################################################

<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/alignment/lux> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "HeritageGraph–LUX alignment (Linked Art / CIDOC-CRM)"@en ;
    dct:description "Class- and property-level mapping from CAIR Nepal HeritageGraph to LUX, the Yale Linked Art / CIDOC-CRM dataset, validated against the official Linked Art JSON-LD context. Version 1.1.0 (November 2026) follows HeritageGraph 1.1.0: no equivalence to or axioms on external terms, conservative over the core (lux-conservativity gate), direct reuse of the 15 CIDOC-CRM classes the core reuses, and terms it mints marked rdfs:isDefinedBy."@en ;
    dct:creator "Semih Yumuşak" , "Niraj Karki" ;
    dct:license <https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0> ;
    rdfs:comment "Licensed under Apache-2.0 (the heritagegraph-lux-migration folder), unlike the core ontology (CC BY 4.0). Terms in the HeritageGraph namespace that this module mints are marked rdfs:isDefinedBy this module."@en ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/alignment/lux/1.1.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.1.0" ;
    owl:imports <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/ontology> .

#####################################################################
# 1. CLASS-LEVEL ALIGNMENT
#    Pattern:  <HG class> rdfs:subClassOf <CRM class> .  (no equivalences to external classes)
#    Comment column shows the LUX JSON-LD alias.
#####################################################################

# ---- Direct equivalents (semantically identical) ----------------------------

hg:HistoricalEvent rdfs:subClassOf crm:E5_Event .  # LUX alias: "Event"


# ---- Architectural / object hierarchy ---------------------------------------
# In LUX every building is crm:E22 classified_as a Type. We keep HG subclasses
# but assert subClassOf crm:E22 so a LUX consumer sees them as objects.

hg:ArchitecturalStructure rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .

hg:ArchitecturalElement rdfs:subClassOf crm:E25_Human-Made_Feature ;  # LUX alias: "HumanMadeFeature"
    skos:closeMatch crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .

hg:Temple rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .
hg:Stupa rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .
hg:Chaitya rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .
hg:Pati rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .
hg:Sattal rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .
hg:Dharmashala rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .
hg:RestHouse rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .
hg:DhungeDhara rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .
hg:Pokhari rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .
hg:WaterStructure rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .

hg:IconographicObject rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .
hg:Murti rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .
hg:Paubha rdfs:subClassOf crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .

# Union class — closeMatch (LUX has no union analogue)
hg:PhysicalHeritageThing skos:closeMatch crm:E22_Human-Made_Object .

# ---- Group / actor ----------------------------------------------------------

hg:Guthi rdfs:subClassOf crm:E74_Group .  # LUX alias: "Group"
hg:CasteGroup rdfs:subClassOf crm:E74_Group .
hg:DataCustodian rdfs:subClassOf crm:E39_Actor .

# ---- Activities / events ----------------------------------------------------

hg:RitualEvent rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .  # LUX alias: "Activity"

hg:Festival rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .
hg:ChariotFestival rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .
hg:MaskedDance rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .

hg:Consecration rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .
hg:Enshrinement rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .
hg:KumariSelectionEvent rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .
hg:KumariRetirementEvent rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .

hg:KumariTenure rdfs:subClassOf crm:E4_Period .  # LUX alias: "Period"

# ---- Documentation / source -------------------------------------------------

hg:DocumentationActivity rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .

hg:FieldSurveyActivity rdfs:subClassOf sci:S4_Observation .

hg:OralHistoryInterview rdfs:subClassOf crm:E65_Creation .  # LUX alias: "Creation"

hg:Verification rdfs:subClassOf crm:E13_Attribute_Assignment .  # LUX alias: "AttributeAssignment"

hg:DataSource rdfs:subClassOf crm:E73_Information_Object .  # LUX alias: "InformationObject"
hg:InformationObject rdfs:subClassOf crm:E73_Information_Object .

hg:FieldSurveyDataset rdfs:subClassOf crm:E31_Document .  # LUX alias: "Document"
hg:OralHistoryRecording rdfs:subClassOf crm:E33_Linguistic_Object .  # LUX alias: "LinguisticObject"
hg:ArchivalRecord rdfs:subClassOf crm:E31_Document .

# ---- Provenance / assertion -------------------------------------------------

hg:SyncreticRelationship rdfs:subClassOf crm:E13_Attribute_Assignment .
hg:AssertionSubject skos:broadMatch crm:E1_CRM_Entity .  # fixed June 2026 (Niraj) — E1 is crm:, not crminf:

# ---- Concepts / types -------------------------------------------------------

hg:ReligiousTradition rdfs:subClassOf crm:E55_Type .  # LUX alias: "Type"

hg:DatePrecision rdfs:subClassOf crm:E55_Type .
hg:ConditionType rdfs:subClassOf crm:E55_Type .
hg:ExistenceStatus rdfs:subClassOf crm:E55_Type .
hg:GuthiType rdfs:subClassOf crm:E55_Type .
hg:RitualType rdfs:subClassOf crm:E55_Type .
hg:SyncreticType rdfs:subClassOf crm:E55_Type .

# ---- Container / metadata ---------------------------------------------------
# HeritageGraph 1.1.0 deprecates hg:Container and hg:Metadata:
# they are LinkML serialization constructs for JSON/YAML data files (defined only in
# HeritageGraph-container.yaml), not domain classes, so the module maps neither.

#####################################################################
# Conservativity (October 2026): loaded with CIDOC-CRM, a mapping must not give
# HeritageGraph data a CRM type that contradicts CIDOC-CRM (E2 Temporal Entity is
# disjoint from E77 Persistent Item; E18 Physical Thing vs E28 non-material
# Conceptual Object) nor a core class the core does not entail. Property mappings
# whose CRM domain or range violated this are skos:closeMatch below
# (evaluation/reasoning_extras.py lux-conservativity checks it).
#####################################################################
# 2. PROPERTY-LEVEL ALIGNMENT
#    Aligned to the crm: URIs LUX expands its short names to.
#####################################################################

# ---- Agent / participation --------------------------------------------------

hg:performedByGroup rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P14_carried_out_by .
hg:performsRitual rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P14i_performed .
# hadParticipant is used on KumariTenure, which is deliberately not a crm:E5_Event
# (broad-matched to crm:E4_Period). P11's domain is E5 Event, so an equivalence would
# type every tenure with a participant as an event once merged with CIDOC-CRM.
# Non-logical link instead.
hg:hadParticipant skos:closeMatch crm:P11_had_participant .  # LUX alias: "participant"
hg:invokesDeity rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of .
hg:isInvokedInRitual rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P12i_was_present_at .

# ---- Place / time -----------------------------------------------------------

# 1.1.0: was rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P55_has_current_location, which asserted a
# lost structure's hypothesised location as its current location. A
# hypothesis is not a fact: related match only (a hypothesis with its
# evidence is a crminf:I2 belief about a P53 location).
hg:hypothesizedLocation skos:relatedMatch crm:P55_has_current_location .

# ---- Composition / parts ----------------------------------------------------


# ---- Material / technique / type --------------------------------------------

hg:hasArchitecturalStyle rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P2_has_type .  # LUX alias: "classified_as"
hg:hasConditionType rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P2_has_type .
hg:hasReligiousTradition rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P2_has_type .
hg:guthiType rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P2_has_type .
hg:ritualType rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P2_has_type .
hg:placeType rdfs:seeAlso crm:P2_has_type .
hg:custodianType rdfs:seeAlso crm:P2_has_type .
hg:syncreticType rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P2_has_type .
hg:datePrecision rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P2_has_type .
hg:existenceStatus rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P2_has_type .

# ---- Production / destruction / custody / title -----------------------------

hg:destructionEvent owl:equivalentProperty crm:P13i_was_destroyed_by .  # LUX alias: "destroyed_by"
hg:transferredToGuthi rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P29_custody_received_by .

# ---- Membership -------------------------------------------------------------

hg:managedByGuthi skos:relatedMatch crm:P49_has_former_or_current_keeper .  # LUX alias: "current_keeper"; P49 domain E18 would make managed rituals physical things

# ---- Aboutness / depiction --------------------------------------------------


hg:isAboutDeity skos:closeMatch crm:P138_represents .  # P138 domain E36 would make a Murti a visual item

# ---- Sequencing -------------------------------------------------------------


# ---- Documentation linkage --------------------------------------------------

hg:mentionedInSource rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by .  # LUX alias: "referred_to_by"; ⊑ not ≡: mentionedInSource (range DataSource) is narrower than P67i
# 1.1.0: was skos:closeMatch crm:P94i_was_created_by (documenting is not creating);
# now the same match as the core: a survey that records something observes it.
hg:documentedBy skos:closeMatch sci:O8i_was_observed_by .  # this module's CRMsci namespace (LUX data uses sci:); the core uses the cidoc-crm.org one

# ---- Person life events (better expressed as Birth/Death events) ------------

hg:birthTimespan skos:closeMatch crm:P4_has_time-span ;  # P4 domain E2 would make a person a temporal entity
    rdfs:comment "Better modeled via crm:P98i_was_born (LUX alias 'born') -> crm:P4_has_time-span."@en .

hg:deathTimespan skos:closeMatch crm:P4_has_time-span ;  # P4 domain E2 would make a person a temporal entity
    rdfs:comment "Better modeled via crm:P100i_died_in / crm:P93i_was_taken_out_of_existence_by + timespan."@en .

hg:publicationTimespan skos:closeMatch crm:P4_has_time-span .  # P4 domain E2 would make a source a temporal entity

# ---- Identification / labelling --------------------------------------------

hg:sourceCitation rdfs:seeAlso crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by .

#####################################################################
# 3. NEW HERITAGEGRAPH CLASSES PROPOSED FOR INTEROPERABILITY
#    Each is rooted in the actual URI LUX uses (mostly crm:; only la:Set
#    and friends are genuine la: classes per Linked Art's JSON-LD context).
#####################################################################

hg:Group a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "obsolete Group"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Generic group of actors (LUX alias: 'Group'). Superseded by crm:E74_Group."@en ;
    owl:deprecated true ;
    dct:isReplacedBy crm:E74_Group ;
    skos:editorialNote "Deprecated in 1.1.0: HeritageGraph 1.1.0 reuses crm:E74_Group directly as its Group class (super-class of Guthi and CasteGroup), so LUX groups are migrated as crm:E74_Group by direct URI reuse (§6). This wrapper is kept only so that data minted by earlier versions still resolves."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E74_Group .

hg:Birth a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Birth"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Birth event of a Person; carries timespan, place, and parent attributions. LUX alias: 'Birth'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E67_Birth .

hg:Death a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "obsolete Death"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Death event of a Person (LUX alias: 'Death'). Superseded by crm:E69_Death."@en ;
    owl:deprecated true ;
    dct:isReplacedBy crm:E69_Death ;
    skos:editorialNote "Deprecated in 1.1.0: HeritageGraph 1.1.0 reuses crm:E69_Death directly as its Death class, so LUX deaths are migrated as crm:E69_Death by direct URI reuse (§6). This wrapper is kept only so that data minted by earlier versions still resolves."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E69_Death .

hg:Formation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Formation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Founding event of a Guthi/Group. LUX alias: 'Formation'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E66_Formation .

hg:Dissolution a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Dissolution"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Termination event of a Guthi/Group. LUX alias: 'Dissolution'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E68_Dissolution .

hg:Acquisition a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Acquisition"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Title transfer (vs. custody only). LUX alias: 'Acquisition'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E8_Acquisition .

hg:Move a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Move"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Physical movement of an object — distinct from custody change. LUX alias: 'Move'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E9_Move .

hg:VisualItem a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Visual Item"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Iconographic content separate from the physical Murti/Paubha. LUX alias: 'VisualItem'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E36_Visual_Item .

hg:LinguisticObject a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Linguistic Object"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Textual content — inscriptions, manuscripts, transcribed oral history. LUX alias: 'LinguisticObject'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E33_Linguistic_Object .

hg:DigitalObject a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Digital Object"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Photographs, 3D scans, audio recordings. LUX alias: 'DigitalObject' (note: LUX uses CRMdig dig:D1, not crmdig:)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf dig:D1_Digital_Object .

hg:Set a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Set"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Curated grouping. LUX alias: 'Set' — this is one of the genuine la: classes (la:Set), not a CRM class. Linked Art deliberately mints la:Set distinct from crm:E78_Curated_Holding to allow ad-hoc groupings."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf la:Set ;
    skos:closeMatch crm:E78_Curated_Holding .

hg:CuratedHolding a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Curated Holding"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Formally curated holding (museum collection, library set). LUX alias: 'CuratedHolding'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E78_Curated_Holding .

hg:Identifier a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Identifier"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Catalogue numbers, DANAM IDs, DOIs. LUX alias: 'Identifier'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E42_Identifier .

hg:Name a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Name"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Multilingual name. LUX alias: 'Name' → crm:E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation (multi-instantiated)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation .

hg:MeasurementUnit a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Measurement Unit"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E58_Measurement_Unit .

hg:Dimension a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Dimension"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Height/width/depth/weight values. LUX alias: 'Dimension'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E54_Dimension .

hg:Right a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Right"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Access/IP rights on photographs and datasets. LUX alias: 'Right'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E30_Right .

hg:LegalObject a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Legal Object"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Things subject to legal frameworks — e.g. 'Ancient Monument' under Nepal heritage law. LUX alias: 'LegalObject'. (HG previously called this 'LegalConcept' which is not a Linked Art class; renamed for compatibility.)"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E72_Legal_Object .

hg:AttributeAssignment a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Attribute Assignment"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Generic super-class above Verification / SyncreticRelationship / Measurement / IdentifierAssignment / TypeAssignment (the core's Assertion, crminf:I2_Belief, is not under it). LUX alias: 'AttributeAssignment'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E13_Attribute_Assignment .

hg:Verification rdfs:subClassOf hg:AttributeAssignment .
hg:SyncreticRelationship rdfs:subClassOf hg:AttributeAssignment .

hg:Period a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Period"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Generic historical period (Licchavi, Malla, Shah, Rana). LUX alias: 'Period'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E4_Period .

hg:KumariTenure rdfs:subClassOf hg:Period .

hg:Encounter a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Encounter Event"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Field encounter / rediscovery of a heritage object. LUX alias: 'Encounter' → CRMsci sci:S19_Encounter_Event (NOT crm:E87 Curation Activity)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf sci:S19_Encounter_Event .

hg:CurationActivity a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Curation Activity"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Conservation / inventory / accession activities by a museum or Guthi. LUX alias: 'CurationActivity' → crm:E87."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E87_Curation_Activity .

hg:ProvenanceActivity a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Provenance Activity"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Wrapper for chains of custody / ownership / movement events. LUX models this as crm:E7_Activity classified_as a 'provenance' Type — NOT a separate la: class. Migration: LUX provenance activities land here as crm:E7_Activity instances."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .

# ---- Additions for full LUX → HG migration coverage ------------------------

hg:Modification a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Modification"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Restoration or alteration of a Murti/Temple/artifact. LUX alias: 'Modification'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E11_Modification .

hg:Language a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Language"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Language of a Name or LinguisticObject (Devanagari, Nepali, Newari, Sanskrit, English). LUX alias: 'Language'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E56_Language .

hg:Currency a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Currency"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Monetary unit referenced in Acquisition/Payment activities. LUX alias: 'Currency'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E98_Currency .

hg:MonetaryAmount a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Monetary Amount"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Amount of money. LUX alias: 'MonetaryAmount'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E97_Monetary_Amount .

hg:BeginningOfExistence a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Beginning of Existence"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Generic existence-start event when no specific Production/Birth/Formation applies. LUX alias: 'BeginningOfExistence'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E63_Beginning_of_Existence .

hg:EndOfExistence a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "End of Existence"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Generic existence-end event (mirror). LUX alias: 'EndOfExistence'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E64_End_of_Existence .

hg:PropositionalObject a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Propositional Object"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Abstract works, doctrines, beliefs — separate from any physical carrier. LUX alias: 'PropositionalObject'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E89_Propositional_Object .

hg:Measurement a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Measurement"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Act of measuring an object's dimension. LUX alias: 'Measurement'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E16_Measurement .

hg:Inscription a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Inscription"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Inscriptions on stone/metal/manuscripts. LUX alias: 'Inscription'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E34_Inscription .

hg:Title a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Title"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Titled name of a work or object. LUX alias: 'Title'."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E35_Title .

#####################################################################
# 4. INTERNAL HG HIERARCHY & PROPERTIES FOR NEW CLASSES
#
#    Without this section, the new classes from Section 3 only
#    sit under external CRM/Linked-Art URIs and appear as orphans
#    when the HG ontology is viewed on its own (Niraj, June 2026).
#    This section wires every new class into the existing HG graph
#    via (a) HG-internal rdfs:subClassOf links and (b) object
#    properties whose domain and range are HG classes.
#####################################################################

# ---- 4.1  Existence-event hierarchy (CRM E63/E64 tree mirrored in HG) -----

hg:Birth rdfs:subClassOf hg:BeginningOfExistence .
hg:Formation rdfs:subClassOf hg:BeginningOfExistence .

hg:Death rdfs:subClassOf hg:EndOfExistence .
hg:Dissolution rdfs:subClassOf hg:EndOfExistence .

# ---- 4.2  Curation / activity hierarchy -----------------------------------

hg:Modification rdfs:subClassOf hg:CurationActivity .

hg:Acquisition rdfs:subClassOf hg:ProvenanceActivity .
hg:Move rdfs:subClassOf hg:ProvenanceActivity .

# ---- 4.3  Identification / linguistic hierarchy ---------------------------

hg:Title rdfs:subClassOf hg:Name .  # E35 ⊏ E33_E41
hg:Inscription rdfs:subClassOf hg:LinguisticObject .  # E34 ⊏ E33

# ---- 4.4  Information-object hierarchy ------------------------------------

hg:DigitalObject rdfs:subClassOf hg:InformationObject .
hg:LinguisticObject rdfs:subClassOf hg:InformationObject .
hg:PropositionalObject rdfs:subClassOf hg:InformationObject .
# Metadata ⊑ hg:InformationObject removed: the core has InformationObject ⊑ DataSource, so it made all
# metadata a DataSource (a new subsumption between core classes). Metadata ⊑ crm:E73 was removed too
# when the core deprecated Metadata (1.1.0, §1).

# ---- 4.5  Curated holding / set -------------------------------------------

hg:Set rdfs:subClassOf hg:CuratedHolding ;
    rdfs:comment "Linked Art mints la:Set distinct from crm:E78 to allow ad-hoc groupings. Within HG we additionally treat Set as a CuratedHolding for navigation; no semantic collapse — both parents remain."@en .

# ---- 4.6  Actor hierarchy --------------------------------------------------

hg:DataCustodian rdfs:subClassOf crm:E39_Actor .

# ---- 4.7  Object properties wiring new classes to existing HG graph -------

# --- Descriptive properties of a physical heritage thing --------------------

hg:carriesInscription a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "carries inscription"@en ;
    rdfs:domain crm:E22_Human-Made_Object ;
    rdfs:range hg:Inscription ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P128_carries .

hg:hasDimension a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has dimension"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:PhysicalHeritageThing ;
    rdfs:range hg:Dimension ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P43_has_dimension .

hg:hasVisualItem a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "shows visual item"@en ;
    rdfs:domain crm:E22_Human-Made_Object ;
    rdfs:range hg:VisualItem ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P65_shows_visual_item .

hg:hasDigitalRepresentation a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has digital representation"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:PhysicalHeritageThing ;
    rdfs:range hg:DigitalObject ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P138i_has_representation .

hg:hasRight a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has right"@en ;
    rdfs:range hg:Right .

# 1.1.0: no longer rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by, whose
# range is E89 Propositional Object: a LegalObject is an E72, which includes
# physical things, so a physical legal object became a conceptual one
# (inconsistent under E18/E28 disjointness). Kept as a related match until
# the legal-status modelling (crm:E30 Right, P104) is decided.
hg:subjectToLegalObject a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "subject to legal status"@en ;
    rdfs:range hg:LegalObject ;
    skos:relatedMatch crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by .

# --- Identification ---------------------------------------------------------

hg:identifiedByIdentifier a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "identified by identifier"@en ;
    rdfs:range hg:Identifier ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P1_is_identified_by .

hg:identifiedByName a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "identified by name"@en ;
    rdfs:range hg:Name ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P1_is_identified_by .

# 1.1.0: was rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P102_has_title, whose domain is E71
# Human-Made Thing (a persistent item): a titled ritual, tenure or event
# became both a temporal entity and a persistent item. A Title is an E35
# and so an E41 Appellation: crm:P1_is_identified_by (E1 to E41), of which
# P102 is itself a subproperty.
hg:identifiedByTitle a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has title"@en ;
    rdfs:range hg:Title ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P1_is_identified_by .

# --- Lifecycle events linking individuals & groups to event nodes ----------

hg:wasBornBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "was born by"@en ;
    rdfs:domain crm:E21_Person ;
    rdfs:range hg:Birth ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P98i_was_born .

hg:diedInEvent a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "died in event"@en ;
    rdfs:domain crm:E21_Person ;
    rdfs:range crm:E69_Death ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P100i_died_in .

hg:wasFormedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "was formed by"@en ;
    rdfs:domain crm:E74_Group ;
    rdfs:range hg:Formation ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P95i_was_formed_by .

hg:dissolvedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "dissolved by"@en ;
    rdfs:domain crm:E74_Group ;
    rdfs:range hg:Dissolution ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P99i_was_dissolved_by .

# --- Object-history events --------------------------------------------------

hg:wasModifiedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "was modified by"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:PhysicalHeritageThing ;
    rdfs:range hg:Modification ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P31i_was_modified_by .

hg:wasMovedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "was moved by"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:PhysicalHeritageThing ;
    rdfs:range hg:Move ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P25i_moved_by .

hg:wasAcquiredThrough a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "was acquired through"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:PhysicalHeritageThing ;
    rdfs:range hg:Acquisition ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P24i_changed_ownership_through .

hg:wasEncounteredIn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "was encountered in"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:PhysicalHeritageThing ;
    rdfs:range hg:Encounter ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf sci:O19i_was_object_encountered_at .

hg:wasMeasuredBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "was measured by"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:PhysicalHeritageThing ;
    rdfs:range hg:Measurement ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P39i_was_measured_by .

# --- Measurement / monetary internal wiring --------------------------------

hg:measurementObserves a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "measurement observes"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:Measurement ;
    rdfs:range hg:Dimension ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P40_observed_dimension .

hg:dimensionHasUnit a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "dimension has unit"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:Dimension ;
    rdfs:range hg:MeasurementUnit ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P91_has_unit .

hg:amountInCurrency a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "amount in currency"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:MonetaryAmount ;
    rdfs:range hg:Currency ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P180_has_currency .

hg:acquisitionAmount a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "acquisition amount"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:Acquisition ;
    rdfs:range hg:MonetaryAmount ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P179_had_sales_price .

# --- Language --------------------------------------------------------------

hg:hasLanguage a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has language"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:LinguisticObject ;
    rdfs:range hg:Language ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P72_has_language .

# --- Set / curated-holding membership --------------------------------------

hg:memberOfSet a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is member of set"@en ;
    rdfs:range hg:Set .

# 1.1.0: range narrowed from AssertionSubject (which includes events, roles
# and sources) to crm:E18_Physical_Thing: crm:P46_is_composed_of is physical
# composition (E18 to E18), so every item held was entailed a physical thing,
# making a ritual or a data source "held" in a holding an E18.
hg:holdsItem a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "holds item"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:CuratedHolding ;
    rdfs:range crm:E18_Physical_Thing ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P46_is_composed_of .

# --- Period containment ----------------------------------------------------

hg:occursDuringPeriod a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "occurs during period"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:RitualEvent ;
    rdfs:range hg:Period ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P10_falls_within .

# --- Propositional object / doctrine ---------------------------------------

# 1.1.0: was rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P129_is_about, the reverse direction.
# P129 runs from the propositional object (E89) to what it is about, so the
# subject of aboutProposition (any heritage subject: a temple, a ritual) was
# entailed an E89 Propositional Object, a conceptual object. The heritage
# subject is the subject of the proposition: crm:P129i_is_subject_of.
hg:aboutProposition a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is subject of proposition"@en ;
    rdfs:range hg:PropositionalObject ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P129i_is_subject_of .

# --- Metadata on any heritage thing ----------------------------------------

hg:hasMetadata a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has metadata"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Range is crm:E73_Information_Object: the core's hg:Metadata is deprecated in HeritageGraph 1.1.0 (a JSON/YAML serialization construct)."@en ;
    rdfs:range crm:E73_Information_Object ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by .

# --- DataCustodian role ----------------------------------------------------

hg:hasDataCustodian a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has data custodian"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range hg:DataCustodian ;
    skos:closeMatch crm:P109_has_current_or_former_curator .  # P109 domain E78 would make a DataSource a physical holding

# --- Container: not mapped (deprecated LinkML serialization construct, HeritageGraph 1.1.0) ---

#####################################################################
# 5. COVERAGE & TAXONOMY COMPLETION (July 2026 gap audit)
#
#    Two gap families closed here:
#    (a) LUX classes with NO HG target — six of the seven genuine la:
#        classes (only la:Set was mapped) plus crm:/sci: classes that
#        occur as @type in LUX data at full scale (Purchase, Joining,
#        Leaving, BiologicalObject, Mark, Site, …). Any of these firing
#        V1 would hard-fail a full-scale migration run.
#    (b) Section-3 classes that §4 wired only via OBJECT PROPERTIES
#        (domain/range edges) but not taxonomically — 20 classes had
#        no HG-internal rdfs:subClassOf parent. They are re-parented
#        below with CRM-consistent internal edges.
#
#    Deliberate HG roots after this section (documented, not orphans):
#    hg:Period (temporal top), hg:Concept (conceptual top),
#    hg:Dimension (value-space top), hg:LegalObject (legal top).
#####################################################################

# ---- 5.1  Structural super-classes -----------------------------------------

hg:Activity a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "obsolete Activity"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Generic intentional activity (LUX alias: 'Activity'). Superseded by crm:E7_Activity."@en ;
    owl:deprecated true ;
    dct:isReplacedBy crm:E7_Activity ;
    skos:editorialNote "Deprecated in 1.1.0: HeritageGraph 1.1.0 reuses crm:E7_Activity directly as its generic activity class (GenericActivity), so LUX activities that match no more specific class are migrated as crm:E7_Activity by direct URI reuse (§6), and the module's activity classes sit directly under crm:E7_Activity. This wrapper is kept only so that data minted by earlier versions still resolves."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .

hg:Concept a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Concept"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Conceptual/type top — landing class for LUX crm:E55_Type concept records (/data/concept/). Deliberate HG root."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E55_Type .

hg:Appellation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Appellation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Names, identifiers and other appellations. LUX alias: 'Appellation' → crm:E41."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E41_Appellation .

hg:Creation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Creation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Creation of an information object (non-physical). LUX alias: 'Creation' → crm:E65. CRM: E65 ⊏ E7 ∧ E63, mirrored internally."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E65_Creation ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:BeginningOfExistence .

# ---- 5.2  The six missing genuine la: classes -------------------------------

hg:Payment a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Payment"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Monetary payment inside a provenance activity. LUX alias: 'Payment' → la:Payment (genuine la: class, ⊏ crm:E7 per Linked Art ontology)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf la:Payment ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:ProvenanceActivity .

hg:Transfer a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Transfer"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Generic transfer of an object between actors when neither title nor custody change is asserted. LUX alias: 'Transfer' → la:Transfer (genuine la: class)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf la:Transfer ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:ProvenanceActivity .

hg:SetAddition a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Addition (to set)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Addition of a member to a la:Set (accession into a collection). LUX alias: 'Addition' → la:Addition (genuine la: class). Named SetAddition in HG to avoid confusion with crm:E79_Part_Addition (hg:PartAddition)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf la:Addition ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:CurationActivity .

hg:SetRemoval a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Removal (from set)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Removal of a member from a la:Set (deaccession). LUX alias: 'Removal' → la:Removal (genuine la: class). Mirror of hg:SetAddition."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf la:Removal ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:CurationActivity .

hg:RightAcquisition a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Right Acquisition"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Acquisition of a Right (copyright, access) over a thing. LUX alias: 'RightAcquisition' → la:RightAcquisition (genuine la: class)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf la:RightAcquisition ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:ProvenanceActivity .

hg:DigitalService a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Digital Service"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Access service for digital content (IIIF image/presentation endpoints on virtually every LUX digital record). LUX alias: 'DigitalService' → la:DigitalService (genuine la: class). Treated as an InformationObject in HG."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf la:DigitalService ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:InformationObject .

# ---- 5.3  crm:/sci: classes seen in LUX data but previously unmapped --------

hg:Purchase a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Purchase"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Acquisition with a sales price. LUX alias: 'Purchase' → crm:E96 (⊏ E8, mirrored internally)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E96_Purchase ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:Acquisition .

hg:Joining a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Joining"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Actor joining a Group (Linked Art models group membership changes via E85/E86). LUX alias: 'Joining' → crm:E85."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E85_Joining ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .

hg:Leaving a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Leaving"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Actor leaving a Group. LUX alias: 'Leaving' → crm:E86. Mirror of hg:Joining."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E86_Leaving ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .

hg:TypeCreation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Type Creation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Creation of a new Type/concept (taxonomy minting). LUX alias: 'TypeCreation' → crm:E83 (⊏ E65, mirrored internally)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E83_Type_Creation ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:Creation .

hg:IdentifierAssignment a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Identifier Assignment"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Assignment of an Identifier to an entity. LUX alias: 'IdentifierAssignment' → crm:E15 (⊏ E13)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E15_Identifier_Assignment ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:AttributeAssignment .

hg:TypeAssignment a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Type Assignment"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Assignment of a Type to an entity. LUX alias: 'TypeAssignment' → crm:E17 (⊏ E13)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E17_Type_Assignment ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:AttributeAssignment .

hg:PartAddition a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Part Addition"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Physical part added to an object. LUX alias: 'PartAddition' → crm:E79 (⊏ E11, mirrored internally). Distinct from hg:SetAddition (la:Addition)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E79_Part_Addition ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:Modification .

hg:PartRemoval a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Part Removal"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Physical part removed from an object. LUX alias: 'PartRemoval' → crm:E80 (⊏ E11)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E80_Part_Removal ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:Modification .

hg:Transformation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Transformation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "One thing ends, another begins (e.g. fragment → relic). LUX alias: 'Transformation' → crm:E81 (⊏ E63 ∧ E64, mirrored internally)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E81_Transformation ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:BeginningOfExistence ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:EndOfExistence .

hg:BiologicalObject a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Biological Object"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Natural-history specimen (LUX includes Yale Peabody Museum records). LUX alias: 'BiologicalObject' → crm:E20. Internal parent hg:PhysicalHeritageThing is pragmatic (specimens as heritage-collection objects) — CRM-wise E20 ⊏ E19, not E22."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E20_Biological_Object ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:PhysicalHeritageThing .

hg:PhysicalFeature a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Physical Feature"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Physical feature attached to an object or site. LUX alias: 'PhysicalFeature' → crm:E26. Internal parent hg:PhysicalHeritageThing is pragmatic."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E26_Physical_Feature ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:PhysicalHeritageThing .

hg:Site a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Site"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Delimited natural/built site. LUX alias: 'Site' → crm:E27 (⊏ E26, mirrored internally). NOTE: CRM Site is a physical thing, NOT an E53 Place."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E27_Site ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:PhysicalFeature .

hg:Mark a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Mark"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Hallmarks, stamps, maker's marks. LUX alias: 'Mark' → crm:E37 (⊏ E36, mirrored internally)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E37_Mark ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:VisualItem .

hg:AuthorityDocument a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Authority Document"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Vocabulary/authority source document referenced by LUX concept records. LUX alias: 'AuthorityDocument' → crm:E32 (⊏ E31)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E32_Authority_Document ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:DataSource .

hg:ProductType a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Product Type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Industrial product model/type. LUX alias: 'ProductType' → crm:E99 (⊏ E55, mirrored internally)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E99_Product_Type ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:Concept .

hg:Presence a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Presence"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Temporal slice of a thing/period at a place (used in LUX provenance/exhibition modeling). LUX alias: 'Presence' → crm:E93. Internal parent hg:Period is PRAGMATIC ONLY — CRM-wise E93 ⊏ E92 Spacetime Volume (sibling of E4); flagged for two-rater review."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf crm:E93_Presence ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:Period .

# ---- 5.4  Internal re-parenting of §3 classes (taxonomy completion) ---------
# §4 connected these via object properties only; the subClassOf edges below
# make each class reachable in the HG-only CLASS HIERARCHY view as well.

hg:VisualItem rdfs:subClassOf hg:InformationObject .  # E36 ⊏ E73
hg:Name rdfs:subClassOf hg:LinguisticObject ;  # E33_E41 ⊏ E33 ∧ E41
    rdfs:subClassOf hg:Appellation .
hg:Identifier rdfs:subClassOf hg:Appellation .  # E42 ⊏ E41
hg:CuratedHolding rdfs:subClassOf hg:PhysicalHeritageThing .  # E78 ⊏ E24 (pragmatic HG parent)
hg:CurationActivity rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .  # E87 ⊏ E7
hg:ProvenanceActivity rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .  # E7-classified
hg:AttributeAssignment rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .  # E13 ⊏ E7
hg:Encounter rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity ;  # S19 ⊏ S4 ⊏ E13 ⊏ E7 (flattened)
    rdfs:comment "Parent flattened to crm:E7_Activity; the full CRMsci chain S19 ⊏ S4_Observation ⊏ E13 would land it under hg:AttributeAssignment — kept simpler for HG navigation."@en .
hg:Measurement rdfs:subClassOf hg:AttributeAssignment .  # E16 ⊏ E13
hg:BeginningOfExistence rdfs:subClassOf hg:HistoricalEvent .  # E63 ⊏ E5
hg:EndOfExistence rdfs:subClassOf hg:HistoricalEvent .  # E64 ⊏ E5
hg:HistoricalEvent rdfs:subClassOf hg:Period .  # E5 ⊏ E4 (CRM-exact)
hg:MonetaryAmount rdfs:subClassOf hg:Dimension .  # E97 ⊏ E54
hg:Right rdfs:subClassOf hg:PropositionalObject .  # E30 ⊏ E89
hg:Language rdfs:subClassOf hg:Concept .  # E56 ⊏ E55
hg:Currency rdfs:subClassOf hg:Concept .  # E98 ⊏ E55
hg:MeasurementUnit rdfs:subClassOf hg:Concept .  # E58 ⊏ E55
hg:Inscription rdfs:subClassOf hg:Mark .  # E34 ⊏ E33 ∧ E37

# Concept-branch classes gathered under hg:Concept for HG-only navigation:
hg:ReligiousTradition rdfs:subClassOf hg:Concept .

# Main-ontology orphans spotted during the same audit (same §4 pattern):
hg:Consecration rdfs:subClassOf hg:RitualEvent .
hg:Enshrinement rdfs:subClassOf hg:RitualEvent .
hg:ArchitecturalElement rdfs:subClassOf hg:PhysicalFeature .  # E25 ⊏ E26

# Documented deliberate roots (no HG-internal parent BY DESIGN):
hg:Period rdfs:comment "Deliberate HG root: temporal top (crm:E4). Children: HistoricalEvent, KumariTenure, Presence."@en .
hg:Dimension rdfs:comment "Deliberate HG root: value-space top (crm:E54). Child: MonetaryAmount."@en .
hg:LegalObject rdfs:comment "Deliberate HG root: legal-framework top (crm:E72 has no natural HG parent)."@en .

# ---- 5.5  Object properties wiring the new classes (§4 pattern) ------------

hg:paidAmount a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "paid amount"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:Payment ;
    rdfs:range hg:MonetaryAmount ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf la:paid_amount .

hg:paidFrom a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "paid from"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:Payment ;
    rdfs:range crm:E39_Actor ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf la:paid_from .

hg:paidTo a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "paid to"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:Payment ;
    rdfs:range crm:E39_Actor ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf la:paid_to .

hg:transferredThing a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "transferred thing"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:Transfer ;
    rdfs:range hg:PhysicalHeritageThing ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf la:transferred .

hg:digitallyAvailableVia a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "digitally available via"@en ;
    rdfs:domain hg:DigitalObject ;
    rdfs:range hg:DigitalService ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf la:digitally_available_via .

# NOTE — abstract CRM supers (E1, E2, E18, E19, E24, E70, E71, E77, E90, E92)
# remain deliberately unmapped: LUX never uses them as @type on instances;
# they exist in the JSON-LD context only for property-range completeness.
# V1 will therefore not fire on them.


#####################################################################
# 6. ALPHA5 CORE-ONTOLOGY SYNC (July 2026)
#
#    Source: CAIRNepal/heritagegraphontology, branch `HeritageGraph`,
#    ontology/HeritageGraph.{yaml,ttl}, "GENERATED ... alpha5 ... on
#    2026-07-22" (commit chain incl. ff1a1ac6 "Fixed the ontology and
#    verified using Hermit and OOPS", 2026-07-16). This is the branch
#    our tooling actually tracks (`main` has been stale since Feb 2026
#    — see server-bootstrap.sh Bug 8 note); this repo's fetch scripts
#    were not yet pointed at `HeritageGraph` before this sync.
#
#    What changed upstream: for classes whose meaning is already fully
#    covered by an external vocabulary term, HeritageGraph.yaml now sets
#    `class_uri` directly to that external URI instead of minting a new
#    hg: resource related to it by owl:equivalentClass. The
#    LinkML → OWL generator therefore emits the class ONLY under the
#    external URI. Concretely, these 12 former HeritageGraph classes no
#    longer exist as separate hg: resources in the core ontology — the
#    crm: URI IS the class:
#
#      HumanMadeObject      → crm:E22_Human-Made_Object
#      Person               → crm:E21_Person
#      Actor                → crm:E39_Actor
#      Place                → crm:E53_Place
#      TimeSpan             → crm:E52_Time-Span
#      Material             → crm:E57_Material
#      Production           → crm:E12_Production
#      DestructionEvent     → crm:E6_Destruction
#      TransferOfCustody    → crm:E10_Transfer_of_Custody
#      ConditionAssessment  → crm:E14_Condition_Assessment
#      ConditionState       → crm:E3_Condition_State
#      Technique            → crm:E29_Design_or_Procedure
#
#    (Three more classes moved the same way but were never referenced by
#    name in this alignment file, so nothing to change for them: Entity →
#    prov:Entity, Activity → prov:Activity, Agent → prov:Agent — all
#    abstract PROV-O tops.)
#
#    1.1.0 (November 2026): the 1.1.0 core reuses three more CRM classes
#    directly: crm:E74_Group (Group, super-class of Guthi and CasteGroup),
#    crm:E69_Death (Death) and crm:E7_Activity (GenericActivity). The same
#    rule therefore applies to them: LUX groups, deaths and generic
#    activities are migrated as the CRM classes, and the module's own
#    wrappers hg:Group, hg:Death and hg:Activity are owl:deprecated with
#    dct:isReplacedBy the CRM class. Module classes that had hg:Activity
#    as parent now sit directly under crm:E7_Activity; the properties
#    wasFormedBy / dissolvedBy (domain) and diedInEvent (range) use the
#    CRM classes.
#
#    Fix applied here: every owl:equivalentClass / skos:closeMatch /
#    rdfs:subClassOf axiom that related one of the 12 hg:
#    URIs above to its crm: counterpart became a tautology (X relates to
#    X) once the hg: URI was substituted for the crm: URI —
#    13 such lines were removed. All rdfs:domain / rdfs:range
#    declarations on object properties (§4, §5.5) and all rdfs:subClassOf
#    statements that used one of these 12 classes as SUBJECT (e.g.
#    hg:DataCustodian rdfs:subClassOf the former hg:Actor) were
#    rewritten to the crm: URI. The companion files were updated the same
#    way — see ../queries/lux_to_hg_migration.sparql and
#    ../scripts/migrate_lux_to_hg.py (TRANSFORM_TEMPLATES): every CONSTRUCT
#    / INSERT arm that minted `a hg:<one of the 12>` on a new
#    /imported/lux/ node now mints `a crm:E..` directly instead.
#
#    Not in scope here: the ~25 Nepal-domain classes added upstream in
#    the same alpha5 pass (KumariHouse, ChariotFestival, Guthi-adjacent
#    ritual/selection-criterion classes, etc.) have no LUX counterpart
#    and are intentionally NOT added to this file — this alignment only
#    covers the LUX ↔ HG bridge, not HG's native domain coverage.
#####################################################################

# ---- 6.1  Schema-level coverage marker for the direct-URI-reuse classes ----
#
# (12 classes from the alpha5 sync plus, in 1.1.0, crm:E74_Group,
# crm:E69_Death and crm:E7_Activity: 15 in total.)
#
# V1 (validation_queries.sparql) originally proved coverage by finding an
# alignment-graph triple relating a hg:-prefixed subject to the
# LUX class. That test can no longer fire for the 12 classes above (there is
# no hg: URI left to be the subject). A first fix made V1 instead
# check for *any instance* of the LUX class already present in
# imported/lux — but that is DATA-dependent: under a bounded pilot run
# (LIMIT_PER_QUERY), a genuinely-covered class can have zero migrated
# instances just from sampling, which produced 3 false V1 failures on the
# first post-alpha5 deploy (2026-07-26: E52_Time-Span, E12_Production,
# E57_Material — all legitimately handled by the transform templates, just
# not sampled into this particular limited run).
#
# Fix: an explicit, SCHEMA-level (not instance-level) coverage marker below,
# true regardless of run size. V1/t11 check this in addition to (not instead
# of) the imported/lux instance check.
hg:alignmentLuxDirectlyReuses a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/alignment/lux> ;
    rdfs:label "directly reuses (no hg: wrapper)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Declares that a LUX/CRM class is migrated by direct URI reuse (§6) rather than via an owl:equivalentClass/subClassOf edge to a hg: class. Used by V1_unmapped_lux_classes as a schema-level coverage proof that does not depend on how many instances a given pilot run happened to migrate."@en .

<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/alignment/lux>
    hg:alignmentLuxDirectlyReuses
        crm:E22_Human-Made_Object, crm:E21_Person, crm:E39_Actor,
        crm:E53_Place, crm:E52_Time-Span, crm:E57_Material,
        crm:E12_Production, crm:E6_Destruction, crm:E10_Transfer_of_Custody,
        crm:E14_Condition_Assessment, crm:E3_Condition_State,
        crm:E29_Design_or_Procedure,
        crm:E74_Group, crm:E69_Death, crm:E7_Activity .


